These are **hard invariants** for Ceti. Apply them in every change.

## Product

- Ceti is a **B2B2C educational SaaS** sold to **private schools in Colombia**.
  The buyer is the school; what it pays for is **curricular compliance
  (CONPES 4005) + teacher reporting + saved teacher time**, delivered through a
  gamified financial-education experience for students (13+).
- Every feature must justify itself against compliance/reporting/teacher-time.
  "It's fun for the student" is not, by itself, a reason to build something.

## Multi-tenancy & roles (core invariant)

- Tenancy hierarchy: **`colegio → (sede, optional in MVP) → curso → estudiante`**.
  `sede` is modeled but optional in MVP; do not block on it.
- Roles: `rector`/`coordinador` (whole school / their sede), `profesor` (their
  courses only), `estudiante` (their own experience only).
- Authorization is driven by **custom claims** (`role`, `colegioId`, and a
  `sedeId` when present) on the Firebase Auth token, set by a Cloud Function —
  **never** trusted from client-writable Firestore fields.
- `firestore.rules` enforces the hierarchy from day one. A teacher can read a
  student's progress **only** because a rule authorizes it by role+tenant — never
  by per-user grants bolted on later.

## NOT the family model (forbidden — regression if reintroduced)

- The old **parent/child financial-guardianship** model was removed and stays
  removed. Forbidden: `parent`/`child`/`family` entities, routes, stores, repos;
  any "child profile" owned by another app user; any guardian acting as an
  in-app user with a dashboard over a minor.
- The institutional hierarchy (school staff ↔ students) is **org-tenancy, not
  guardianship** — do not model it with the old family primitives.
- The **acudiente** (legal guardian) exists **only** as a consent signer in the
  Ley 1581 authorization flow. They are not an app role, have no login-as-parent
  dashboard, and see no other student's data.

## Compliance — Ley 1581 / Decreto 1377 (blocking)

- Processing a minor's data requires **acudiente authorization** before the
  student account is activated. A student without recorded authorization stays
  in `pendiente_autorizacion` and inactive.
- **Minimize PII**: students are keyed by a **school-provided pseudonym/ID**, not
  by personal name/email/age, wherever possible. Never write a minor's name,
  email, or age outside what the authorization flow strictly requires.
- Maintain a **register of authorizations** (timestamp + version) and support
  **data suppression** (deletion) on request.
- A **data-treatment policy** must be linked in-app.
- `MIN_AGE = 13` is enforced in `UserSetupScreen`. Do not lower it.
- Analytics params **must not contain user PII**: no `name`, `email`, `age`,
  `nickname`, `fullName`, or any identifier that maps back to a person/minor.
  Route all analytics through `src/shared/lib/analytics/logEvent.ts`.

## Removed / forbidden features

- **No real money**: savings goals are **simulated** with virtual currency.
  No gift cards, no "pay kids to learn", no linking to real bank accounts.
- **No public/global leaderboards** (documented harm to adolescents).
  Class-level collaboration/competition the teacher can toggle is allowed.
- **No generative AI in MVP**: detect "where the course is weak" with **simple
  rules**, not ML. Generative/adaptive question banks are V3+. The human-curated
  question bank stays the source of truth.
- **No B2C freemium funnel** as a priority. The customer is the school.

## Data model

- Tenancy data lives under the institutional tree (see `docs/data-model.md`);
  account-scoped auth data lives under `users/{uid}`.
- **Student progress must be readable by the authorized teacher/rector** — model
  it under the tenant tree (keyed by pseudonymous `studentId`), not buried under
  a private `users/{uid}` subtree the teacher cannot reach.
- **Savings/goals are simulated** (virtual currency). There is no real-money or
  approval/pending workflow on real funds.
- Each **world maps 1:1 to a CONPES 4005 competency** (`competencia` field), so
  the teacher dashboard can show "world = competency".

## Allowed Firestore paths

Defined and constructed exclusively via `src/shared/lib/firebase/paths.ts`. The
authoritative, evolving list lives in `docs/data-model.md`. Any new path requires
three coordinated changes:

1. A helper exported from `src/shared/lib/firebase/paths.ts`.
2. A least-privilege, role-aware rule in `firestore.rules`.
3. A repository under `src/features/<domain>/data/<entity>Repository.ts` that
   uses the helper.

The global `questionBank/{questionId}` stays read-only for signed-in clients;
writes go through the Admin SDK seed script.

## Platform

- **MVP target is web responsive** (Expo Web / React Native Web over this same
  codebase). Keep platform shims in `src/shared/lib/*` (`*.web.ts` /
  `Platform.OS` branches): MMKV→AsyncStorage, native Firebase telemetry→no-op,
  Google sign-in→popup/redirect. Native iOS/Android is **out of scope for MVP** —
  do not invest in EAS native builds, native-only modules, or store flows now.

## Code organization

- **Feature-first.** Domain code lives in `src/features/<domain>/{screens,
  components,data,store,...}`. Cross-feature imports are forbidden — share via
  `src/shared/*`.
- **Firestore paths** via `src/shared/lib/firebase/paths.ts` (see
  `firebase-modular-client.mdc`).
- **Store persistence** via `@shared/lib/storage/mmkv` (see `zustand-stores.mdc`).
- **User-visible strings** via `t('...')`, defined in
  `src/shared/i18n/locales/es.json`.

## Tooling stack

- **State management:** Zustand. **Local persistence:** MMKV (`react-native-mmkv`,
  web falls back to AsyncStorage).
- **Server state:** repository pattern under `src/features/**/data/*Repository.ts`
  against Firestore (JS modular SDK — web-compatible).
- **Styling:** RN `StyleSheet` + theme via `useThemeColors()`.
- **E2E:** Maestro (`e2e/maestro/`).
- **Diagnostics:** Crashlytics/Perf/Analytics via `@react-native-firebase/*` on
  native; **no-op on web**.

## When in doubt

- Changes to `firestore.rules` route through the rules auditor (see `AGENTS.md`)
  and must be tested against the emulator with role/tenant scenarios.
- Changes to analytics, auth, role claims, PII handling, or age handling route
  through the compliance guard (Ley 1581 + COPPA/GDPR-K).
- Before any release, the Maestro smoke must be green.
